     "\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div>\r\n    <p>gathered these, in case you find what you need..<br>\r\n      <br>\r\n      you could denote horizontal intervals via vertical lines using <br>\r\n      - <a href=\"https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/geom_abline.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/geom_abline.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366153951000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1m3mfbnm7EbeVbxViwEqIN\">https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/geom_abline.html</a><br>\r\n      <br>\r\n      geom smooth has a size variable you could perhaps utilise <br>\r\n      <br>\r\n      listing of available geoms <br>\r\n      -\r\n      <a href=\"https://rstudio.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/ggplot2-cheatsheet.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rstudio.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/ggplot2-cheatsheet.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366153951000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1hDOpdC5cJJDxPOYR5TmxI\">https://rstudio.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/ggplot2-cheatsheet.pdf</a><br>\r\n      <br>\r\n      This looks targeted to what you want<br>\r\n      - <a href=\"http://pages.stat.wisc.edu/~larget/stat302/chap3.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pages.stat.wisc.edu/~larget/stat302/chap3.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366153951000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2XENQEYEJz4lDV_-ZoKleK\">http://pages.stat.wisc.edu/~larget/stat302/chap3.pdf</a><br>\r\n      <br>\r\n      and a few other<br>\r\n      -\r\n<a href=\"https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/172189/plot-the-confidence-interval-of-bootstrapping-in-ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/172189/plot-the-confidence-interval-of-bootstrapping-in-ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=179236615395